@participant6 
I don't think the aws sdk version change the directory structure.
Maybe this change comes with the Opensearch upgrade from 2.X to 3.X ?

@participant6 @participant4 Please find 3.2 archive to test here: https://github.com/participant5/OpenSearch/blob/repository-s3-fix-3.2/repository-s3-3.2.0-SNAPSHOT.zip


That archive contains the changes described here: https://github.com/opensearch-project/OpenSearch/issues/18240#issuecomment-3224659260

I'm not sure it will work, but worth a try.

@participant5

It seems you forgot to do the same changes in S3AsyncService.java.
I did the changes, rebuilt the plugin, and it works in my setup.

@participant5 
I only tested with Outscale Object Storage, which is a "S3 like" cloud service.
I think it should be tested with other providers (Minio...) and AWS S3, ton confirm it works in all cases

@participant9 

It works for me with 3.3.0 version.

Though you have to do an extra config to make the connector use "compatibility mode".

@participant5 @participant9  

I thought the parameter was `s3.client.default.legacy_md5_checksum_calculation`, and I had the same error.

I managed to make it working by creating/updating the snapshot repos by API (https://<redacted-host>/latest/api-reference/snapshots/create-repository/) : 

```
{
    "type": "s3",
    "settings": {
        "bucket": "bucketname",
        "base_path": "path_in_bucket",
        "legacy_md5_checksum_calculation": "true"
    }
}
```
